From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek-v4-flash: narrower DSpark drafts for large PP cohorts

VLLM_DSV4_NARROW_DRAFT="W:N" (default unset = unchanged). A PP cohort of at
least N requests drafts only the first W positions of the DSpark block (W
query tokens per request, its own FULL draft graphs captured next to the K=5
ones) and the CPU verification policy caps that cohort's width at W. Draft
ids past W stay stale with confidence 0; the target verifies whatever it is
given, so outputs are unchanged and only acceptance and draft cost move.

At max-num-seqs 32 over PP3 (cohorts of ~11), the K=5 drafter computed 55
query tokens per cohort where a K=3 engine computes 33, and the adaptive
widths fell behind fixed ones (code c32 1423 tok/s vs 1572 at spec_k=4).
Measured at c32 (tok/s, full batch): K=3 engine 1588 / 1382 / 896 (code /
counting / prose); no narrowing 1423-1531 / 1377 / 850-859; W:N = 3:9
1572 / 1284-1304 / 894-913; 4:9 1598 / 1350 / 918. The dsv4-flash profile
sets 4:9; cohorts below 9 requests (c <= 16) are unaffected.

---
diff --git a/vllm/dsv41_opt_profile.py b/vllm/dsv41_opt_profile.py
--- a/vllm/dsv41_opt_profile.py
+++ b/vllm/dsv41_opt_profile.py
@@ -67,6 +67,8 @@
     "VLLM_DSPARK_DRAFT_HEAD_FP8": "1",
     # uniform verification graphs for 12/24-request PP cohorts (0008)
     "VLLM_DSV4_VERIFICATION_COHORTS": "1",
+    # cohorts of >= 9 requests draft and verify at most 4 positions (0009)
+    "VLLM_DSV4_NARROW_DRAFT": "4:9",
     # target decode kernels
     "VLLM_DSV4_FAST_DET_MOE_ALIGN": "1",
     "VLLM_DSV4_CUDA_DET_ALIGN": "1",
